findings.remediation:
Either grant the binding inside the module (requires project number, so add a data source):

  data "google_project" "current" {
    project_id = var.project_id
  }

  resource "google_kms_crypto_key_iam_member" "cloud_run_cmek" {
    crypto_key_id = var.encryption_key
    role          = "roles/cloudkms.cryptoKeyEncrypterDecrypter"
    member        = "serviceAccount:service-${data.google_project.current.number}@serverless-robot-prod.iam.gserviceaccount.com"
  }

or, if the module intentionally treats the CMEK key as caller-owned and out of scope (the same stance it already takes for Bigtable IAM), document the required grant on the encryption_key variable description and in the example, the way backup_job_service_account_email already documents the Bigtable grant.
